{
  "description": "Prop expression parity cases generated by @json-render/core (resolvePropValue, resolveElementProps, resolveBindings). Each case: { \"name\", \"fn\", \"state\", ...input, \"expected\", \"undefined\"?, \"undefinedPaths\" }. fn \"resolvePropValue\": input \"value\" (any JSON). expected = resolvePropValue(value, { stateModel: state }). When core returns undefined, \"expected\" is null and \"undefined\": true. fn \"resolveElementProps\": input \"props\" (object). expected = resolveElementProps(props, { stateModel: state }); \"bindings\" = resolveBindings(props, ctx) (prop name -> state path, or null when there are none). JSON has no undefined: inside objects a key that resolves to undefined is omitted, inside arrays it becomes null. \"undefinedPaths\" lists JSON Pointers (relative to the result; \"\" is the result itself) of every value core resolved to undefined, so consumers can tell undefined from null: an object key in undefinedPaths is present-but-undefined in core (and omitted from \"expected\"); an array index in undefinedPaths is undefined in core (and null in \"expected\"). Empty when the result contains no undefined. $item/$index/$bindItem/$computed are out of scope for v1: outside a repeat (and without functions) core resolves them to undefined.",
